      "title": "fresh: Terminal based IDE & text editor: easy, powerful and fast",
      "url": "https://github.com/sinelaw/fresh",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/yhfmtx",
      "score": 4,
      "comments": 6,
      "author": "linkdd",
      "published": "2026-09-12T11:59:21Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Positions as an out-of-the-box terminal IDE, competing with Helix and Neovim by minimizing complex configuration overhead.",
        "Targets low-latency TUI workflows with built-in Language Server Protocol (LSP) support and structured syntax tree parsing.",
        "Streamlines remote SSH and container development without requiring heavyweight graphical clients or Electron-based runtimes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Linux Zoom Client Proactively Reads X11 Clipboard",
      "url": "https://hachyderm.io/@simontatham/117201594980991062",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/8t1ddm",
      "score": 11,
      "comments": 5,
      "author": "darleaf",
      "published": "2026-09-12T12:38:53Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Zoom's Linux client continuously polls the X11 clipboard without user interaction, potentially exfiltrating copied credentials, secrets, or sensitive text.",
        "The behavior exploits legacy X11's lack of clipboard isolation, where any connected desktop application can read global clipboard buffers unrestricted.",
        "Mitigate exposure by switching to Wayland for per-window clipboard boundaries, sandboxing Zoom via Flatpak, or using the web client."
      ]
    },
